'''''The Traitors''''' (also known as '''''The Traitors US''''' outside of the United States) is an American [[reality competition]] series based on the [[Netherlands|Dutch]] series ''[[De Verraders]].''

Following the premise of ''De Verraders'', the show features a group of contestants participating in a [[social deduction game]] similar to [[Mafia (party game)|Mafia or Werewolf]], set in and among the grounds of [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]] in Scotland. During the game, a small group of contestants become the titular "Traitors", and work together to eliminate the other contestants to win a grand prize, while the remaining contestants become "Faithful" and are tasked to discover and banish the Traitors by voting to eliminate them to win the grand prize. While the first season featured civilian contestants and reality television personalities, subsequent seasons exclusively featured reality television personalities and other celebrities.

It is hosted by Scottish actor [[Alan Cumming]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 22, 2022 |title=Alan Cumming To Host Psychological Competition Series 'The Traitors' For Peacock |url=https://deadline.com/2022/04/alan-cumming-host-psychological-competition-series-the-traitors-peacock-1235012369/ |access-date=January 13, 2023 |website=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref> The first season was released on [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]] on January 12, 2023. In February 2023, the series was renewed for a second season, and the first three episodes were released on January 12, 2024.<ref name="Renewed">{{Cite web |last=Tinoco |first=Armando |date=February 2, 2023 |title='The Traitors' Renewed For Season 2 At Peacock As Andy Cohen Hosts Season 1 Reunion Special |url=https://deadline.com/2023/02/the-traitors-renewed-season-2-peacock-plus-season-1-reunion-hosted-andy-cohen-1235247773/ |access-date=February 2, 2023 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Thompson |first=Cher |date=2024-01-12 |title=The Traitors US Season 2 Full Schedule - When New Episodes Release, What Time & How To Watch |url=https://screenrant.com/the-traitors-us-season-2-when-new-episodes-release-what-time-how-watch/ |access-date=2024-01-13 |website=ScreenRant |language=en}}</ref> In February 2024, the show was renewed for a third season.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/the-traitors-renewed-season-3-peacock-1235901022/ | title='The Traitors' Renewed for Season 3 at Peacock | date=February 7, 2024 }}</ref> In August 2024, the show was renewed for two additional seasons through season 5.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://deadline.com/2024/08/the-traitors-renewed-season-4-5-peacock-1236039834/ | title='The Traitors' Renewed for Seasons 4 & 5 at Peacock | date=August 14, 2024 }}</ref> The fifth season, subtitled ''[[The Traitors (American TV series) season 5|New Blood]],''<ref>{{cite web | url=https://deadline.com/2026/06/the-traitors-new-blood-premiere-date-nbc-civilian-series-1236959387/ | title='The Traitors: New Blood' Sets September Premiere Date On NBC For Civilian Series | date=June 18, 2026 }}</ref> featured the show's first all-civilian cast and premiered on September 17, 2026, on [[NBC]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tinoco |first=Armando |date=2025-08-14 |title=‘The Traitors’ Civilian Version Ordered At NBC With Alan Cumming As Host |url=https://deadline.com/2025/08/the-traitors-civilian-version-nbc-alan-cumming-host-1236489064/ |access-date=2025-08-20 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> The [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 6|sixth season]] will premiere in January 2027, with a new cast of celebrities.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-11 |title= Peacock Showcases Powerhouse Slate at Today's NBCUniversal Upfront |url= https://www.nbcuniversal.com/article/peacock-showcases-powerhouse-slate-todays-nbcuniversal-upfront?fbclid=PAdGRleASeSIFUREVYBG7zMWV4dG4DYWVtAjEwAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDzEyNDAyNDU3NDI4NzQxNAABp509sSbamKzB7xgyAIdON66M2IuekhLmKrKsT0g5S0_tE8FJHjikelXxYjp__aem_rx6ck2EWSB7VFVCpNgUKpA&fbclid=PAdGRleASeV3RleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBzcnRjBmFwcF9pZA8xMjQwMjQ1NzQyODc0MTQAAacQidaE1_Too_XHtL1vJ_KeeRK5T-ee7b6pBsGhMc7Kl9UYg3RrN2Hnnzp2QQ_aem_FCoNEPK1jyJ8PGRAWocJdQ |access-date=2026-06-16 |website=NBCUniversal |language=en-US}}</ref> One day before the season 5 premiere, the show was renewed for three additional seasons through season 9.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.peacocktv.com/blog/the-traitors-ordered-for-three-more-seasons-peacock| title=Peacock Orders The Traitors for 3 More Seasons! (DETAILS)| date=September 16, 2026}}</ref>

==Format==
[[File:Ardross Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1234702.jpg|thumb|upright=1.3|The series was filmed at [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]] in Scotland (pictured in 2003)<ref name="castle">{{Cite web |last=Rhymes |first=Shameika |date=January 17, 2023 |title=Can You Stay At The Scottish Highlands Castle In 'The Traitors?' |url=https://www.usanetwork.com/usa-insider/the-traitors-castle-scottish-highlands |access-date=January 23, 2023 |website=USA Insider Official Site}}</ref>]]
A group of contestants arrive at a castle in the [[Scottish Highlands]] with a goal to win a cash prize that is added through missions. The players are known as the "Faithful" but among them are the "Traitors", a group of contestants selected by the host, whose goal is to eliminate the Faithfuls and claim the prize for themselves. If the Faithful contestants eliminate all the Traitors, they will share the prize fund, but if any Traitors remain at the end, they steal the money.

Most nights, the Traitors come together meeting in the castle "turret" and decide upon one Faithful contestant to "murder" and that person leaves the game immediately. The remaining Faithful contestants do not know who has been eliminated until the following day when that person does not enter the castle for breakfast.

The murders usually occur after the banishments. The group then participate in a mission to add money to the prize fund. Some challenges also offer an opportunity for players to win the "shield" which gives players immunity from being murdered that night, but not from the banishment vote. An attempted murder on the shield holder will result in no player being eliminated.

At the end of most days, the group participates in the Banishment Ceremony, where the players gather at the Round Table to discuss who they want to eliminate before individually voting for a player to banish. Players cast their votes privately before [[Open ballot system|revealing their vote]] in turn to everyone, as they provide a reason for the vote. The person obtaining the [[plurality voting|most votes]] is banished from the game and must reveal their affiliation. Starting from season three, banished players do not reveal their affiliation on the final day. In a tied vote, a run-off vote occurs between those tied with the highest vote tallies. For [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 5|season 5]], if the players banished a Traitor, they would add $15,000 to the pot.

When a Traitor is eliminated, the host sometimes gives the remaining Traitors the opportunity to recruit another player.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-01-09 |title=The Traitors: What You Need to Know About How the Game Works |url=https://www.peacocktv.com/blog/the-traitors-game-rules |access-date=2026-04-25 |website=Peacock |language=en-US}}</ref>

===End Game===

Once the game has reached the final four, the remaining players participate in the final challenge. The players are given a choice to "Banish Again" or to "End Game." A unanimous "End Game" vote concludes the game, while a single vote to "Banish Again" results in another banishment vote, followed by another choice between "Banish Again" or "End Game". When the game ends, if all remaining players are Faithful, then the prize money is divided evenly among them. However, if any Traitors remain, they win the entire pot.

