== International broadcasts ==
In the United Kingdom, the series was acquired by the BBC as a companion to its [[The Traitors (British TV series)|British version]], with episodes released on [[BBC iPlayer]] the day after the American release, January 13, 2023, and linear television airings for [[BBC Three]] and [[BBC One]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=January 12, 2023 |title=BBC acquires The Traitors US |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2023/bbc-acquires-the-traitors-us/ |access-date=January 15, 2023 |website=BBC}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldbart |first=Max |date=February 3, 2023 |title='The Traitors' U.S. Premiere Becomes Most-Watched BBC Three Show Since Linear Relaunch |url=https://deadline.com/2023/02/the-traitors-us-bbc-three-ratings-peacock-alan-cumming-1235248791/ |access-date=February 3, 2023 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> However, since 2024, the series was moved to air in late January as the BBC moved the British version to early January, typically airing in the same slot on [[BBC Three]] as the British version.

In [[Australia]], the series was made available to stream on [[10 (VoD service)|10 Play]] in March 2023, as a companion to the [[The Traitors (Australian TV series)|Australian version]] broadcast by [[Network 10]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=March 23, 2023 |title=Sleep with One Eye Open: Traitors US and Traitors UK Now Available on 10 Play |url=https://10play.com.au/10-play-trending/articles/sleep-with-one-eye-open-traitors-us-and-traitors-uk-now-available-on-10-play/tpa230322bnyij}}</ref> Starting in 2026, the Peacock edition featuring celebrities is billed in Australia as ''The Celebrity Traitors US,''<ref>https://10.com.au/the-celebrity-traitors-us</ref> while the civilian ''New Blood'' season is billed as ''The Traitors US''.<ref>https://10.com.au/the-traitors-us</ref>

In [[Canada]], the show is available to stream on [[Crave (streaming service)|Crave]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 9, 2023 |title=U.K., U.S. & Australian Versions of "The Traitors" Now Streaming on Crave |url=https://www.memorabletv.com/news/u-k-u-s-australian-versions-of-the-traitors-now-streaming-on-crave/}}</ref> The [[The Traitors Canada|Canadian version]] of the series premiered on October 2, 2023 on [[CTV Television Network|CTV]].<ref>{{cite press release|url=https://www.bellmedia.ca/the-lede/press/trust-no-one-suspect-everyone-casting-revealed-for-new-ctv-original-reality-series-the-traitors-canada-beginning-oct-2/|title=Trust No One. Suspect Everyone. Casting Revealed for New CTV Original Reality Series The Traitors Canada, Beginning Oct. 2|work=[[Bell Media]]|date=September 18, 2023|access-date=September 21, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230921195731/https://www.bellmedia.ca/the-lede/press/trust-no-one-suspect-everyone-casting-revealed-for-new-ctv-original-reality-series-the-traitors-canada-beginning-oct-2/|archive-date=September 21, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

The series, as well as the British, Flemish and Australian versions of the show, are currently available to stream on Videoland in the Netherlands.

== Companion series ==
=== ''The Traitors Postmortem'' ===
During the [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 2|second season]], a [[Web series|web program]] titled ''The Traitors Postmortem'' was introduced, an after-show program featuring additional footage and interviews with eliminated contestants, episodes were released on [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]] and on Peacock's YouTube channel.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nbc.com/nbc-insider/the-traitors-season-2-trailer-premiere-date|title=The Traitors Season 2 Trailer Teases "Betrayal, Sabotage & Murder" with an All-Star Celebrity Cast|work=[[NBC]]|first=Caitlin|last=Busch|date=December 14, 2023|access-date=December 15, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215035946/https://www.nbc.com/nbc-insider/the-traitors-season-2-trailer-premiere-date|archive-date=December 15, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== ''The Traitors Official Podcast'' ===
With the [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 4|season 4]] premiere, a companion podcast titled ''The Traitors Official Podcast'' was introduced and hosted by [[The Traitors (American TV series) season 3|season 3]] contestants [[Rob Mariano]] and [[Bob the Drag Queen]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta|first=Emily|date=2026-01-05|title=‘The Traitors’ Sets Official Companion Podcast Hosted by Boston Rob Mariano and Bob the Drag Queen (EXCLUSIVE)|url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/the-traitors-podcast-boston-rob-bob-the-drag-queen-1236622684/|access-date=2026-03-29|website=Variety|language=en-US}}</ref> The podcast premiered on January 8, 2026, with weekly releases of audio and video episodes produced by USG audio. The podcast features guest interviews with the eliminated contestants each episode.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-05|title=Peacock Reveals The Traitors Official Podcast with 2 Fan Favorites as Hosts (DETAILS)|url=https://www.peacocktv.com/blog/traitors-official-podcast-date-hosts-how-to-listen-watch|access-date=2026-03-29|website=Peacock|language=en-US}}</ref>

== Production ==
To emphasize the show's authentic Scottish Highlands setting at Ardross Castle, production utilizes live traditional musicians to frame dramatic events, missions, and contestant arrivals. Among the local musicians featured on-screen is James Mackenzie, Dingwall, a veteran bagpiper from Ross and Cromarty who performs with the Alness Pipe Band. Known for his mastery of traditional pibroch (classical pipe music), Mackenzie is dressed in traditional Highland attire, including the Mackenzie tartan, to provide the show's distinct, tense auditory backdrop.{{Citation needed|date=September 2026}}

The American show is a sister show to the [[The Traitors (British TV series)|British version]], with both being produced by [[Studio Lambert]] for the [[BBC]] and Peacock. They both feature the same location, props, and missions, with the main difference being the hosts and the contestants.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bryan |first=Scott |date=January 12, 2023 |title='The Traitors' Was a Sensation in Britain. Can It Conquer the U.S.? |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/12/arts/television/the-traitors-us-show.html |access-date=July 12, 2023 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

== Reception ==
=== Television ratings ===
''The Traitors'' became the number one original reality series on the streamer,<ref name="Renewed"/> with the premiere of the season being BBC Three's most-watched show since the relaunch of its [[Broadcast programming|linear television channel]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2023/02/the-traitors-us-bbc-three-ratings-peacock-alan-cumming-1235248791/|title='The Traitors' U.S. Premiere Becomes Most-Watched BBC Three Show Since Linear Relaunch|work=[[Deadline (website)|Deadline]]|first=Max|last=Goldbart|date=February 3, 2023|access-date=December 18, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230520024205/https://deadline.com/2023/02/the-traitors-us-bbc-three-ratings-peacock-alan-cumming-1235248791/|archive-date=May 20, 2023|url-status=live}}</ref>

